gcm/live-draw: RSX_INTERNAL_SCALE, the internal resolution scale switch (1 or 2, default 1), read and validated; not
active yet.

Purpose (issue #55, step 2 of the internal resolution scale, first patch of it): one switch for the internal scale,
shared with the other port, read in one place and checked before anything depends on it. ENHANCEMENT: the PS3 game
always renders at its own resolution.

Change:
- libs/video/rsx_internal_scale.h: rsx_iscale_parse_switch(), the text of a scale switch. Unset or empty = 1x; "1"
  or "2", optionally followed by x or X, with spaces or tabs around. Anything else (0, 3 and above, fractions, signs,
  trailing text, long digit strings) is refused with RSX_ISCALE_E_FACTOR and leaves 1x. Still standard C only, and it
  names no switch: reading the variable is the caller's business. RSX_ISCALE_SWITCH_MAX (2) is the largest scale
  accepted; arbitrary and fractional scales are for a later step.
- rsx_live_draw.c: ld_iscale_requested() reads RSX_INTERNAL_SCALE once, when live-draw starts, and logs one [iscale]
  line: the scale, or that a value was refused (rendering at 1x). The switch is documented there with its default.
  ld_iscale() stays native: a requested 2x logs that the scaled path is not in this build yet and renders at 1x. It
  goes live in a later patch of this series, together with the scaled allocation and the native-size guards at every
  guest-visible boundary, so that the game never sees anything but its own resolution.
- Nothing else reads the switch: allocation, raster state, shaders, pipeline keys and PSO template records are as
  after patch 2300.

Verification: tools/runtime/test_internal_scale_map.sh. The switch text: the accepted forms give 1x or 2x, 17 invalid
forms are refused and leave 1x, and both accepted scales compose with the 1x1, 2x1 and 2x2 AA grids. Wiring checks:
RSX_INTERNAL_SCALE is read once, parsed by the header, read at start and marked ENHANCEMENT:; ld_iscale() is still
native. rsx_live_draw.c compiled with MinGW-w64 gcc 16.2 at -O2 -Wall -Wextra. No game run.

Written for this port; not taken from RPCS3 or any other emulator.

diff -ruN a/libs/video/rsx_internal_scale.h b/libs/video/rsx_internal_scale.h
--- a/libs/video/rsx_internal_scale.h	2026-11-13 13:21:12.236729800 -0800
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_internal_scale.h	2026-11-13 15:02:00.877751300 -0800
@@ -182,4 +182,34 @@
     return rsx_iscale_target_from_sample(sample, aa, scale, out);
 }
 
+/* The scales a renderer may be asked for: 1x and 2x, the same factor on both axes. Arbitrary and fractional scales
+ * are not accepted yet. */
+#define RSX_ISCALE_SWITCH_MAX 2u
+
+/* Parses the text of an internal-scale switch: absent or empty = 1x; "1", "2", optionally followed by "x" or "X",
+ * with surrounding spaces or tabs. Anything else (another number, a fraction, a sign, trailing text) is refused with
+ * RSX_ISCALE_E_FACTOR, and *out is set to 1x so a caller that only logs the refusal renders at the native size.
+ * Reading the variable is the caller's business; this function names no switch. */
+static inline rsx_iscale_status rsx_iscale_parse_switch(const char* text, rsx_iscale_grid* out)
+{
+    *out = rsx_iscale_native();
+    if (!text) return RSX_ISCALE_OK;
+    const char* p = text;
+    while (*p == ' ' || *p == '\t') p++;
+    if (!*p) return RSX_ISCALE_OK;
+    uint32_t v = 0;
+    int digits = 0;
+    while (*p >= '0' && *p <= '9') {
+        if (v > RSX_ISCALE_SWITCH_MAX) return RSX_ISCALE_E_FACTOR;   /* long input: stop before it can wrap */
+        v = v * 10u + (uint32_t)(*p - '0');
+        p++; digits++;
+    }
+    if (!digits) return RSX_ISCALE_E_FACTOR;
+    if (*p == 'x' || *p == 'X') p++;
+    while (*p == ' ' || *p == '\t') p++;
+    if (*p || v < 1u || v > RSX_ISCALE_SWITCH_MAX) return RSX_ISCALE_E_FACTOR;
+    *out = rsx_iscale_grid_make(v, v);
+    return RSX_ISCALE_OK;
+}
+
 #endif /* RSX_INTERNAL_SCALE_H */
diff -ruN a/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c b/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
